*---------------------------------------------------------------
* zp.equ -- liba's private zero-page window.
* Full design notes: L.ZPE.TXT (docs/a2/)
*---------------------------------------------------------------
PTR0        equ   $E0            ;2 bytes -- pointer arg 1 (e.g.
                                 ;src/path/buf)
PTR1        equ   $E2            ;2 bytes -- pointer arg 2 (e.g.
                                 ;dst)
PTR2        equ   $E4            ;2 bytes -- pointer arg 3
                                 ;(SC_SPAWN's fdactions only)
OPTPTR      equ   $EC            ;2 bytes -- getopt.s: the
                                 ;permitted-letters string.
                                 ;Needs ZP because the validity
                                 ;scan is (OPTPTR),y
* -- U2DEC (num.s) working cells. Not meant for use outside
* num.s, but not -- enforced -- nothing in this toolchain
* enforces module-private state.
U2DEC_VAL   equ   $E6            ;2 bytes -- remaining value
                                 ;being converted
U2DEC_SUB   equ   $E8            ;2 bytes -- current power-of-
                                 ;ten subtrahend
U2DEC_DIGIT equ   $EA            ;1 byte  -- digit accumulator
                                 ;for current position
U2DEC_LZ    equ   $EB            ;1 byte  -- leading-zero-
                                 ;suppression flag
* -- stdio.s (docs/PROCIO.md sec 4) working cells. Transient
* -- scratch only -- never holds state across two separate
* -- PUTC/flush calls -- so sharing these two pairs between
* -- SIO_PUTC's own addressing and SIO_CPY's LC-bank1<->stage
* -- copy is safe (SIO_PUTC never re-enters while SIO_CPY holds
* -- them: SIO_PUTC calls SIO_FLUSH, which calls SIO_CPY, all
* -- single-threaded, no reentrancy). (zp),Y indirect addressing
* -- requires zero page, same reason PTR0-PTR2 exist above.
STG_PTR     equ   $EE            ;2 bytes -- source pointer
                                 ;(PUTC: the LC bank1 byte slot;
                                 ;SIO_CPY: the LC bank1 copy
                                 ;source)
* -- RESERVED, NOT AVAILABLE: process zero page $FF is owned by
* -- the KERNEL (inc/entry.frame.equ's K_LCBANK). The syscall
* and
* -- IRQ doors write the interrupted process's language-card
* bank
* -- there, in that process's own zero page, and the exit paths
* -- read it back to restore it. A program that uses $FF will
* have
* -- its LC bank silently mis-restored after any preemption.
* -- docs/LANGUAGE-CARD.md. Highest cell any program claims
* today
* -- is PLASMA's LDPTR at $F9-$FA (src/bin/plasma.s).
ZP_KRN_LCBANK equ $FF            ;= entry.frame.equ's K_LCBANK
DST_PTR     equ   $F0            ;2 bytes -- SIO_CPY's stage-
                                 ;buffer copy destination
*---------------------------------------------------------------
* CONSTANTS THAT ARE NOT ZERO PAGE, and why they live in a file
* whose name says otherwise.
*
* Merlin-8 REJECTS a forward reference to an `equ` -- merlin32
* accepts one silently, so the tree grew several
* (learning:01M05519PC55WGJNE4PY5HX4TH). Each of the constants
* below is DEFINED in a liba module that a program `put`s late
* (seek.s, libabss.s -- libabss.s must be last, it is the
* symbol-anchored dum arena) and USED by code assembled
* earlier. Real Merlin-8 stops with "Illegal forward reference"
* and writes no object; `as` running under maux agrees with it,
* which is how these were found -- file.s, tee.s and time.s
* would not self-host.
*
* They are HERE rather than in a new liba.equ because this file
* is already `put` by all 43 units that `put` libabss.s, always
* in their first equ block. That universality is the property
* the fix needs, and it is safer to reuse the one file that has
* it than to create a second file the next new unit can forget
* -- a miss would assemble cleanly under merlin32 and fail only
* under real Merlin, which is exactly the trap being closed.
*---------------------------------------------------------------
* -- seek.s's whence values (docs/FLEET.md, "`>>` and the seek
* -- family"). Used by callers that are assembled before seek.s
* -- itself is put.
SEEK_SET    equ   0
SEEK_CUR    equ   1
SEEK_END    equ   2
* -- pathres.s's PATHRSLV scratch sizes, sized in libabss.s but
* -- referenced by pathres.s and shpath.s, both put BEFORE it.
* -- PRS_BUFSZ is a LITERAL, not MLI_PTH_MAXLN+1: libabss.s is
* -- linked by every program in the tree including harnesses
* -- that never put mli.equ, and a constant they cannot see
* -- fails to assemble for all of them. pathres.s carries an
* -- `err` tripwire comparing the two where mli.equ IS in
* -- scope, so they cannot drift.
PRS_BUFSZ   equ   65
PTB_SRCSZ   equ   40
* -- stdio.s's stage-buffer size (docs/PROCIO.md sec 4; grown
* -- 512 -> 1024 on 2026-08-28 when the stage became the FIRST
* -- fully-buffered fd's own buffer -- see stdio.s SIO_MODEOF's
* -- stage-owner note). Referenced by stdio.s, DEFINED by
* -- libabss.s's `ds` -- which is put after stdio.s, so the
* -- constant must live here or real Merlin-8 rejects the
* -- forward reference (this file's own header rule).
STGSIZE     equ   1024
* -- readdir.s's directory-block size, used by libabss.s's
* -- RD_DIRBUF reservation -- which EVERY program links, readdir
* -- user or not, so the number needs the universal home (the
* -- PRS_BUFSZ argument). Moved from libabss.s 2026-08-29: an
* -- equate a REL module exports is impossible (Merlin-8 ENT is
* -- code labels only); cross-module equates live in equ files.
RD_BLKSZ    equ   512
* -- regex.s's public match registers (ptr pairs) -- referenced
* -- by edsubst.s and sedexec.s. Moved from regex.s 2026-08-29,
* -- same REL rule as RD_BLKSZ above.
RE_MSTART   equ   $CE
RE_MEND     equ   $D0
* -- env.s's '=' in both text conventions (hi-bit and clear),
* -- hoisted here 2026-08-29: shvar.s is put before env.s and
* -- compares against them in immediate operands -- the same
* -- Merlin-8 forward-reference rule as everything above.
ENV_EQHI    equ   $BD
ENV_EQLO    equ   $3D